nufacture, sale, offering for sale, distribution, display, or misrepresentation of Hamaragharr's trademarks constitutes trademark infringement and passing off</li>\n<li>No license, assignment, dealership, distributorship, or resale right is granted unless expressly authorized in writing by Hamaragharr</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>9.2 Copyright Protection (Copyright Act, 1957)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>All original literary, artistic, photographic, audio-visual, and digital works created by Hamaragharr are protected under Section 13 of the Copyright Act, 1957</li>\n<li>Unauthorized copying, printing, scanning, photographing, recording, storage, publication, circulation, or commercial exploitation—both online and offline—is prohibited under Sections 14, 51, and 63 of the Copyright Act, 1957</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>9.3 Criminal Liability &amp; IPC Provisions (Offline + Online Offences)</h4>\n<p>Any unauthorized use, counterfeiting, duplication, resale, rebranding, fraudulent representation, or deceptive use of Hamaragharr's brand name, logo, product identity, packaging, or content—whether digitally or physically—may attract criminal liability, including but not limited to offenses under:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Section 420 IPC – Cheating and dishonestly inducing delivery of property</li>\n<li>Section 403 IPC – Dishonest misappropriation of property</li>\n<li>Section 406 IPC – Criminal breach of trust</li>\n<li>Section 468 IPC – Forgery for the purpose of cheating</li>\n<li>Section 469 IPC – Forgery intended to harm reputation</li>\n<li>Section 482 IPC – Use of false property mark</li>\n<li>Section 486 IPC – Selling goods marked with a counterfeit trademark</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>9.4 Digital &amp; Physical Misuse (IT Act, 2000 &amp; Offline Acts)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Unauthorized access, scraping, duplication, or misuse of digital content or data is punishable under Sections 43 and 66 of the Information Technology Act, 2000</li>\n<li>Unauthorized printing, replication, packaging imitation, physical resale, or circulation of copyrighted or trademarked material in offline markets is punishable under applicable provisions of the Copyright Act, 1957 and IPC</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>9.5 Enforcement, Monitoring &amp; Legal Remedies</h4>\n<p>Hamaragharr reserves the right to take strict civil and criminal action against any individual, reseller, distributor, organization, or entity involved in online or offline infringement, including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Immediate cease-and-desist notices.</li>\n<li>Injunctions and restraining orders.</li>\n<li>Monetary damages and account of profits.</li>\n<li>Seizure, recall, and destruction of counterfeit or infringing goods.</li>\n<li>Recovery of legal fees and enforcement costs.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>10. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</h3>\n<p>To the maximum extent permitted by law:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hamaragharr shall not be liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages</li>\n<li>Our total liability, if any, shall not exceed the amount paid by you for the specific product or service</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Use of our products and services is entirely at your own discretion and risk.</p>\n\n<h3>11. INDEMNIFICATION</h3>\n<p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Hamaragharr, its partners, directors, employees, and affiliates from any claims, damages, losses, or expenses arising from:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your misuse of the website or products.</li>\n<li>Your violation of these Terms.</li>\n<li>Your infringement of third-party rights.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>12. THIRD-PARTY LINKS</h3>\n<p>Our website may contain links to third-party websites. Hamaragharr has no control over and assumes no responsibility for their content, policies, or practices.</p>\n\n<h3>13. MODIFICATION &amp; TERMINATION</h3>\n<p>We reserve the right to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Modify or discontinue any part of the website or services</li>\n<li>Update these Terms at any time without prior notice</li>\n<li>Suspend or terminate user access for violations</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>15. GOVERNING LAW &amp; JURISDI